    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h3><p>Miscellaneous / Force Downloading</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="force-downloading"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#force-downloading"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Force Downloading</h3><p>Sometimes you want to force the browser to download some content instead of displaying it.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Files *.md&gt;
    ForceType application/octet-stream
    Header set Content-Disposition attachment
&lt;/Files&gt;</code></pre><p>Now there is a yang to this yin:</p>
]]></content>
