  <entry>
    <id>https://www.trackawesomelist.com/2015/02/09/</id>
    <title>Htaccess Updates on Feb 09, 2015</title>
    <updated>2015-02-09T16:54:03.000Z</updated>
    <published>2015-02-09T07:30:34.000Z</published>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection / Force HTTPS Behind a Proxy</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="force-https-behind-a-proxy"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#force-https-behind-a-proxy"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Force HTTPS Behind a Proxy</h3><p>Useful if you have a proxy in front of your server performing TLS termination.</p>
<pre><code>RewriteCond %{HTTP:X-Forwarded-Proto} !https
RewriteRule (.*) https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI}</code></pre><h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection / Alias a Single Directory</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="alias-a-single-directory"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#alias-a-single-directory"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Alias a Single Directory</h3><pre><code>RewriteEngine On
RewriteRule ^source-directory/(.*) /target-directory/$1 [R=301,L]</code></pre><h3><p>Security / Deny Access to Hidden Files and Directories</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="deny-access-to-hidden-files-and-directories"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#deny-access-to-hidden-files-and-directories"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Deny Access to Hidden Files and Directories</h3><p>Hidden files and directories (those whose names start with a dot <code>.</code>) should most, if not all, of the time be secured. For example: <code>.htaccess</code>, <code>.htpasswd</code>, <code>.git</code>, <code>.hg</code>...</p>
<pre><code>RewriteCond %{SCRIPT_FILENAME} -d [OR]
RewriteCond %{SCRIPT_FILENAME} -f
RewriteRule "(^|/)\." - [F]</code></pre><p>Alternatively, you can just raise a “Not Found” error, giving the attacker no clue:</p>
<pre><code>RedirectMatch 404 /\..*$</code></pre>]]></content>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://www.trackawesomelist.com/2015/02/09/"/>
    <summary>3 awesome projects updated on Feb 09, 2015</summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>https://www.trackawesomelist.com/2015/01/27/</id>
    <title>Htaccess Updates on Jan 27, 2015</title>
    <updated>2015-01-27T10:37:22.000Z</updated>
    <published>2015-01-27T08:59:36.000Z</published>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection</p>
</h3>
<p>What we are doing here is mostly collecting useful snippets from all over the interwebs (for example, a good chunk is from <a href="https://github.com/h5bp/server-configs-apache" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apache Server Configs (⭐3.3k)</a>) into one place. While we’ve been trying to credit where due, things might be missing. If you believe anything here is your work and credits should be given, let us know, or just send a PR.</p>
<p>Note: It is assumed that you have <code>mod_rewrite</code> installed and enabled.</p>
<h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection / Force www in a Generic Way</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="force-www-in-a-generic-way"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#force-www-in-a-generic-way"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Force www in a Generic Way</h3><pre><code>RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} !^$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} !^www\. [NC]
RewriteCond %{HTTPS}s ^on(s)|
RewriteRule ^ http%1://www.%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L]</code></pre><p>This works for <em>any</em> domain. <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/4916222/htaccess-how-to-force-www-in-a-generic-way" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source</a></p>
<h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection / Force HTTPS</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="force-https"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#force-https"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Force HTTPS</h3><pre><code>RewriteEngine on
RewriteCond %{HTTPS} !on
RewriteRule (.*) https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI}

# Note: It’s also recommended to enable HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS)
# on your HTTPS website to help prevent man-in-the-middle attacks.
# See https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/HTTP_strict_transport_security
&lt;IfModule mod_headers.c&gt;
    # Remove "includeSubDomains" if you don't want to enforce HSTS on all subdomains
    Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000;includeSubDomains"
&lt;/IfModule&gt;</code></pre><h3><p>Rewrite and Redirection / Force Trailing Slash</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="force-trailing-slash"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#force-trailing-slash"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Force Trailing Slash</h3><pre><code>RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} /+[^\.]+$
RewriteRule ^(.+[^/])$ %{REQUEST_URI}/ [R=301,L]</code></pre><h3><p>Security / Disable Directory Browsing</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="disable-directory-browsing"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#disable-directory-browsing"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Disable Directory Browsing</h3><pre><code>Options All -Indexes</code></pre><h3><p>Security / Password Protect a Directory</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="password-protect-a-directory"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#password-protect-a-directory"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Password Protect a Directory</h3><p>First you need to create a <code>.htpasswd</code> file somewhere in the system:</p>
<pre><code>htpasswd -c /home/fellowship/.htpasswd boromir</code></pre><p>Then you can use it for authentication:</p>
<pre><code>AuthType Basic
AuthName "One does not simply"
AuthUserFile /home/fellowship/.htpasswd
Require valid-user</code></pre><h3><p>Security / Password Protect a File or Several Files</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="password-protect-a-file-or-several-files"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#password-protect-a-file-or-several-files"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Password Protect a File or Several Files</h3><pre><code>AuthName "One still does not simply"
AuthType Basic
AuthUserFile /home/fellowship/.htpasswd

&lt;Files "one-ring.o"&gt;
Require valid-user
&lt;/Files&gt;

&lt;FilesMatch ^((one|two|three)-rings?\.o)$&gt;
Require valid-user
&lt;/FilesMatch&gt;</code></pre><h3><p>Miscellaneous / Set PHP Variables</p>
</h3>
<h3 id="set-php-variables"><a class="anchor" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" href="#set-php-variables"><svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M7.775 3.275a.75.75 0 001.06 1.06l1.25-1.25a2 2 0 112.83 2.83l-2.5 2.5a2 2 0 01-2.83 0 .75.75 0 00-1.06 1.06 3.5 3.5 0 004.95 0l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95-4.95l-1.25 1.25zm-4.69 9.64a2 2 0 010-2.83l2.5-2.5a2 2 0 012.83 0 .75.75 0 001.06-1.06 3.5 3.5 0 00-4.95 0l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 004.95 4.95l1.25-1.25a.75.75 0 00-1.06-1.06l-1.25 1.25a2 2 0 01-2.83 0z"></path></svg></a>Set PHP Variables</h3><pre><code>php_value &lt;key&gt; &lt;val&gt;

# For example:
php_value upload_max_filesize 50M
php_value max_execution_time 240</code></pre>]]></content>
